S += section('7', 'Beyond the syllabus', 'Pricing · Causal inference · Adversarial ML')
S += [P('Each question ends in one sentence, backed by a number with an interval. Null results are reported as they are.'), P('7A. Scouting as an investment portfolio: where does the market misprice?', H2),
      P(f"Each summer from {A['seasons'][0]} to {A['seasons'][-1]} a portfolio of 25 pool players is bought at Transfermarkt value (last valuation before the window opens). The return is the realised fee if he was sold for a fee within 24 months, otherwise his value 24 months later. Five portfolios are compared with 10,000 random portfolios of the same size. Section 6 showed that market value matches the engine at the expensive end, so the useful question is where the market is wrong. A hedonic model answers it: regress log market value on the style-neutral profile, age, league, minutes and club tier (R² {f2(HV['r2'])}, {n_(HV['n'])} player-seasons, standard errors clustered by player). The residual is how far a player is priced from what his profile predicts. The \"under-priced\" portfolio buys the 25 most negative residuals, with the model fitted on seasons up to that summer.")]
po = ['Under-priced (hedonic)', 'Best young performer', 'Hazard', 'Shadow Squad', 'Market value', 'Random']
