S += section('9', 'Limitations and conclusion', 'Honest reading')
S += bullets([f"<b>Coverage.</b> {pc(1 - p2['in_pool_share'])} of real elite replacement signings were outside the candidate pool, most from leagues the data does not cover. The all-signings test only includes players who had 900 minutes in the five leagues the season before.",
              f"<b>Sample size.</b> {p2['in_pool_queries']} in-pool elite replacements in eight seasons, {nq} of them unseen; intervals on that task are wide, a single model moves by several points with its seed, and the order of the top methods is not reliable. The all-signings test ({n_(nqa)} queries) is where differences are measured with confidence.",
              f"<b>Transfer records.</b> {pc(1 - p2['feeders_with_transfer_record'], 1)} of feeder-seasons belong to players with no transfer history even after inferring moves from minutes, and are labelled \"no move\". Loans are inferred from move patterns, not from a loan flag. {pc(1 - p2['all_signings_fee_positive_share'])} of signings have no fee above zero recorded.",
              "<b>Market value.</b> Transfermarkt values are crowd estimates; used strictly before the window, they still encode what the crowd expects.",
              "<b>Local Spark.</b> Everything runs in local mode on one machine, on data far smaller than Spark is for."])
S += [Spacer(1, 2), P(f"Reframing the task as \"whom does the club sign\" gives a test the mid-sem lacked: a real decision by a real club. On {n_(nqa)} unseen signings the engine is clearly better than every baseline, with {TA[SSA]['recall@10'] / TA[MV]['recall@10']:.1f} times the top-10 recall of market value. On elite replacements it is level with market value and the hazard score, and the fee split on the large set explains why: clubs paying big fees buy the players everyone already rates, and the engine's edge is below the median fee. The market itself can be read: players priced below what their profile predicts returned {sp_(PO[UP]['mean_return'])} in two years. Moving to an elite club neither cost nor helped a young player on average. The ranker can be gamed with cheap stats, and ignoring them costs nothing. Style translation, ALS club taste and the hidden-gem flag failed under walk-forward fitting.")]

